{
  "about": "Observation dimensions that the stored fields cannot recover (ADR 0001 §2, ADR 0011). distinct: each variant has the same root status and result and the same per-site job status, stored args and stored result as its base, and differs only in the module status, the carried value or the resolved arguments; it must still compare unequal. same: spellings of one observation that must compare equal, because each optional field has a canonical absence. reject: observations whose fields contradict each other. Provenance is policy: the cases test windmill-lite's observation format, with expectations taken from the cited catalogue cases.",
  "distinct": [
    {
      "name": "FX-V2/a: the job succeeds, the module fails, the handler sees the EarlyStopError",
